    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306">

                <pb facs="0379" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg281"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Wu Ting-fang.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Wu</hi>: In accordance with my promise of
                    this morning, I send you herewith copy of the telegram<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d306-f1"/> which I have just dispatched <pb facs="0380" n="282"
                        xml:id="pg282"/> to the United States consul-general at Shanghai. I beg that
                    you will use your best endeavors to impress upon Earl Li the importance and
                    urgency of the communication Mr. Goodnow is directed to make to him.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
